<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>NPVM freight crossing-source comparison</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f2f5f9;color:#19334b;font:14px system-ui,sans-serif}header{background:#142c43;color:white;padding:24px 4vw}header h1{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:27px}header p{margin:0;color:#dce6f0}.wrap{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:22px}.panel{background:white;border-radius:9px;padding:18px;margin:18px 0}.controls{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap}.muted{font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:#536b80}.notice{background:#fff4d8;padding:14px;border-left:4px solid #d99722;line-height:1.7}label{display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:5px}select{padding:8px;font:inherit;border:1px solid #bdcbd9;border-radius:5px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.chart{height:370px}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce5ed;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}h2{font-size:19px}iframe{width:100%;height:1100px;border:0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#2165a1}.downloads{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;line-height:2}.big{font-size:24px;font-weight:700}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px;margin:18px 0}.card{background:#fff;border-radius:9px;padding:18px}@media(max-width:800px){.grid,.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.wrap{padding:12px}}
</style></head><body><header><h1>NPVM freight · interview places versus network links</h1><p>Same sampled NPVM demand and seed · crossing sources compared directly</p></header><main class="wrap">
<div class="notice" id="basis"></div><section class="panel"><h2>Full sampled trip counts</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Crossing source</th><th>All trips</th><th>Domestic</th><th>Entering</th><th>Leaving</th><th>Transit</th><th>Foreign endpoints</th></tr></thead><tbody id="fullCounts"></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">Entering and leaving exclude transit. Each transit OD is one trip and contributes two foreign endpoints. Counts describe the configured sample, without expansion to 100%. Domestic means NPVM model-domestic, including Liechtenstein/enclaves; these source-zone counts are not measured Swiss border passages.</p></section>
<section class="panel controls"><div><label for="scope">Traffic scope for distances and times</label><select id="scope"><option value="international">All international · entering + leaving + transit</option><option value="incoming">Entering only</option><option value="outgoing">Leaving only</option><option value="transit">Transit only</option><option value="domestic">Domestic only</option><option value="all">All freight</option></select></div><p class="muted">Network: major-road access points and OD-specific crossing routing when enabled. Interview: road references weighted by importance and distance, with directional matches.</p></section>
<div class="cards"><div class="card">Network · total straight-line distance (km)<div class="big" id="networkDistance"></div></div><div class="card">Interview · total straight-line distance (km)<div class="big" id="interviewDistance"></div></div><div class="card">Interview − network distance<div class="big" id="distanceDelta"></div><div class="muted" id="distancePercent"></div></div></div>
<section class="panel"><h2 id="summaryTitle">Selected-scope summary</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Statistic</th><th>Network links</th><th>Interview places</th></tr></thead><tbody id="summary"></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">Distances join the generated activity endpoints with straight lines; these are not routed vehicle-kilometres. Foreign coordinates are crossing anchors, rather than original foreign establishments.</p></section>
<div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Trip distance distribution</h2><div class="chart" id="distanceHistogram"></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>Cumulative trip distance</h2><div class="chart" id="distanceCdf"></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>Departure hours</h2><div class="chart" id="departureHours"></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>Foreign endpoint displacement between sources</h2><div class="chart" id="shifts"></div><p class="muted">Paired foreign endpoints for the full international demand. Transit contributes entry and exit. Displacement measures allocation differences for the same sampled agents, not observed error.</p></section></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>Controls and endpoint changes</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tbody id="controls"></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">The comparison verifies that sampled agents and OD zones match. Domestic coordinates and departure times are checked rather than assumed identical.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Crossing locations and traffic allocation</h2><p class="muted">The embedded map has independent source/direction/region controls. Both sources represent the same agents; adding the two scenarios does not give additional demand. Hover labels begin with a point ID; the next line gives its sampled endpoint count. Selecting a source region highlights its actual allocated points. Network is blue; Interview is orange. Matched coordinates do not force the final MATSim link ID.</p><p><a href="crossings.html">Open the crossing map separately</a></p><iframe title="Compare network and interview-place freight crossings" srcdoc="__MAP_HTML__"></iframe></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Download and provenance</h2><div class="downloads"><a href="summary.parquet">Summary</a><a href="endpoint_shifts.parquet">Paired endpoint displacements</a><a href="network_candidates.parquet">Network candidate probabilities</a><a href="interview_candidates.parquet">Interview candidate probabilities</a><a href="network_anchor_counts.parquet">Network crossing counts</a><a href="interview_anchor_counts.parquet">Interview crossing counts</a><a href="network_trips.parquet">Network freight trips</a><a href="interview_trips.parquet">Interview freight trips</a><a href="provenance.json">Provenance</a></div><details><summary>Source settings and prerequisite provenance</summary><pre id="provenance"></pre></details></section>
</main><script>__PLOTLY__</script><script>
'use strict';
const DATA=__DATA__,META=__META__,MODELS=['Network','Interview'],COLORS=META.colors;
const el=id=>document.getElementById(id),fmt=n=>n===null||n===undefined?'—':Number(n).toLocaleString('en-GB',{maximumFractionDigits:2});
function row(parent,values){const tr=document.createElement('tr');for(const v of values){const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=v;tr.append(td);}parent.append(tr);}
function plot(id,data,layout={}){Plotly.react(id,data,{margin:{l:65,r:20,t:20,b:65},paper_bgcolor:'#fff',plot_bgcolor:'#fff',legend:{orientation:'h'},...layout},{responsive:true,displaylogo:false});}
function update(){
 const scope=el('scope').value,selected=m=>DATA.models[m][scope],a=selected('Network'),b=selected('Interview');
 el('networkDistance').textContent=fmt(a.total_distance_km);el('interviewDistance').textContent=fmt(b.total_distance_km);el('distanceDelta').textContent=fmt(b.total_distance_km-a.total_distance_km)+' km';el('distancePercent').textContent=a.total_distance_km?fmt(100*(b.total_distance_km/a.total_distance_km-1))+'% relative to network':'';
 el('summary').replaceChildren();for(const [label,key] of [['Trips','total'],['Foreign endpoints','foreign_endpoints'],['Distinct crossing coordinates used','anchors_used'],['Total straight-line distance (km)','total_distance_km'],['Mean trip distance (km)','mean_km'],['Median trip distance (km)','median_km'],['95th percentile (km)','p95_km'],['Zero-distance trips','zero_distance']])row(el('summary'),[label,fmt(a[key]),fmt(b[key])]);
 // Shared five-kilometre bins come from the analysis helper; the last bin is 500+ km.
 const bins=Array.from({length:101},(_,i)=>i===100?'500+':`${i*5}–${i*5+5}`);
 plot('distanceHistogram',MODELS.map(m=>({name:m,type:'bar',x:bins,y:selected(m).histogram,marker:{color:COLORS[m]}})),{barmode:'group',xaxis:{title:{text:'Straight-line trip distance (km)'},nticks:12},yaxis:{title:{text:'Sampled trips'}}});
 plot('distanceCdf',MODELS.map(m=>({name:m,type:'scatter',mode:'lines',x:selected(m).cdf_x,y:selected(m).cdf_y,line:{color:COLORS[m]}})),{xaxis:{title:{text:'Straight-line trip distance (km)'}},yaxis:{title:{text:'Cumulative share (%)'},range:[0,100]}});
 const hours=[...new Set(MODELS.flatMap(m=>Object.keys(selected(m).hours).map(Number)))].sort((a,b)=>a-b);
 plot('departureHours',MODELS.map(m=>({name:m,type:'bar',x:hours,y:hours.map(h=>selected(m).hours[h]||0),marker:{color:COLORS[m]}})),{barmode:'group',xaxis:{title:{text:'Departure hour'},dtick:2},yaxis:{title:{text:'Sampled trips'}}});
}
for(const model of MODELS){const s=DATA.models[model];row(el('fullCounts'),[model,...['all','domestic','incoming','outgoing','transit'].map(k=>fmt(s[k].total)),fmt(s.international.foreign_endpoints)]);}
const p=DATA.paired;for(const [label,value] of [['Same sampled agents and OD zones',p.same_demand?'Yes':'No'],['Domestic endpoints whose coordinates changed',p.domestic_endpoint_changes],['Trips whose departure time changed',p.departure_time_changes],['Paired foreign endpoints',p.foreign_endpoints],['Foreign endpoints displaced by more than 1 m',p.moved_over_1m],['Mean displacement (km)',p.mean_shift_km],['Median displacement (km)',p.median_shift_km],['95th percentile displacement (km)',p.p95_shift_km]])row(el('controls'),[label,typeof value==='string'?value:fmt(value)]);
plot('shifts',[{type:'histogram',x:DATA.shifts_km,marker:{color:'#6555a1'},nbinsx:45}],{xaxis:{title:{text:'Foreign endpoint displacement (km)'}},yaxis:{title:{text:'Paired foreign endpoints'}}});
el('basis').textContent=`Both runs use the same ${fmt(META.input_downsampling*100)}% sampled NPVM matrices and seed ${META.random_seed}. Source selection changes crossing availability and allocation, not total OD demand. Interview references do not themselves verify truck access. `+META.distance_basis;
el('scope').onchange=update;el('provenance').textContent=JSON.stringify(META,null,2);update();
</script></body></html>
